@* The design's summary bar: a pill pinned near the bottom of the window, offset by ml-40 so it
   sits over the content column rather than the middle of the whole window, carrying the running
   total and the way out of the builder.

   It clears the footer by the design's own 32px, measured from the footer rather than from the
   window: the footer is not in any design, and lifting the pill is the only way both can own the
   bottom edge without one covering the other. That is the one measurement on this page which no
   longer matches the design, and it is deliberate.

   The design draws this button always ready. Here it stays shut until the workspace can be
   rented, which is the one thing added to the design's markup: a native disabled button, which
   the keyboard cannot reach, with the reason as its title. *@
<div class="total-bar hidden lg:flex fixed bottom-[calc(var(--footer-height)_+_2rem)] left-1/2 transform -translate-x-1/2 ml-40 bg-surface-bright rounded-full shadow-ambient px-6 py-3 items-center gap-6 z-40 border border-surface-container-highest">
    <div class="total-bar__amount flex flex-col">
        <span class="text-[10px] text-outline uppercase tracking-wider font-bold">Monthly Total</span>
        <span class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface font-bold">@View.Quote.MonthlySubtotal.Amount.ToString("C")<span class="text-label-md font-label-md text-on-surface-variant">/mo</span></span>
    </div>

    <div class="w-px h-8 bg-surface-container-highest" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <button type="button"
            class="bg-tertiary-container text-on-tertiary-container px-6 py-2 rounded-full font-bold hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
            disabled="@(!View.CanCheckout)"
            aria-disabled="@((!View.CanCheckout).ToString().ToLowerInvariant())"
            title="@(View.CanCheckout ? null : View.BlockingReason)"
            @onclick="OnReady">
        Ready to Rent?
    </button>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public WorkspaceView View { get; set; } = default!;

    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnReady { get; set; }
}
